# Audit Report -- Phase 268: self-reference detector

**Plan**: docs/plan-qor-phase268-self-reference-detector.md (iteration 20)
**Session**: 2026-09-06T2330-049201
**Risk Grade**: L2
**Mode**: adversarial, Option B independent review

## Verdict

**Verdict**: PASS

At iteration 20, after twenty iterations and roughly twenty grounds, every one in
the document and none in the change.

## Reviewer capability disclosure

The independent reviewer held Read, Grep and Glob only for the entire review and
executed nothing, disclosing that on every finding. It verified no figure in this
phase. It authored one of the grounds itself and withdrew an earlier PASS when
the reach question exposed a design defect it had accepted.

## Governance violation

Implementation preceded the audit verdict. The operator ruled that implementation
requires a passing audit with rare if any exceptions and granted none. The seal
proceeds on his instruction to record rather than excuse it. Consequence: the
red-before state of seven tests is not observable on this tree and was taken on
the author's word.

## What the pass covers

The detector change is correct and matches the plan: exact-name comparison, owner
qualification, leftmost-longest capture, monotone widening of the separator. The
tests exist, match the plan's table, and pin three properties that would fail
silently under plausible alternatives -- prefix comparison, name-only comparison,
slash-only separator.

## What it does not cover

No measurement was verified by the reviewer. The document is not established as
clean; the reviewer stopped finding grounds rather than demonstrating none
remain. Reach was audited for the owner skip only, because that is what was
asked; nothing else in this control has had a reach audit.

## Suite

3278 passed, 6 skipped, 4 deselected, 0 failed. Boundary suites 35 passed. The
new-behaviour file run three consecutive times at 13 passed each. Plan-to-source
parity checked at the seal.
